Subject: menu-v2: an item grows with its content

What: the menu item's fixed 28px height becomes a 28px minimum.
Why: a fixed height clips or overlaps any row whose content wraps: a label
longer than the panel, a description line under the label, a caveat. The
row's padding, alignment and single-line height are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/v2/components/menu-v2.css b/src/v2/components/menu-v2.css
index 8d4622aa19..bc5db3abb0 100644
--- a/src/v2/components/menu-v2.css
+++ b/src/v2/components/menu-v2.css
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
   flex-direction: row;
   align-items: center;
   gap: 8px;
-  height: 28px;
+  min-height: 28px;
   padding: 0 12px;
   background: transparent;
   border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
